From: pcbirc
Subject: PCBSETUP SEARCH.C - pointer parameters for the OpenWatcom port
Date: 2026-09-22

Clark's SEARCH.C passes `uniqueunlimited` by C++ reference. Someone changed
the two function definitions to pointers on the pwa153 (Borland) branch but
left the call sites passing by reference, so the file compiled under neither
compiler. The Borland branch has been restored to Clark's references; this
patch keeps the pointer form for the Watcom port, WITH the matching call
sites, which the original change was missing.

Apply to <branch>/SOURCE/UTIL/PCBSETUP/SOURCE/SEARCH.C when the Watcom
program tree exists (delta154 / irc1541).

--- SEARCH.C	(Clark, references)
+++ SEARCH.C	(pointers)
@@ line 345 @@
-static bool near pascal updatelstfiles(char *FileName, uniqueunlimited & FileNameList, bool (near pascal update(DOSFILE *In, DOSFILE *Out))) {
+static bool near pascal updatelstfiles(char *FileName, uniqueunlimited *FileNameList, bool (near pascal update(DOSFILE *In, DOSFILE *Out))) {
@@ line 352 @@
-  if (FileName[0] == 0 || FileNameList.foundinlist(FileName))
+  if (FileName[0] == 0 || FileNameList->foundinlist(FileName))
@@ line 395 @@
-static bool near pascal scancnames(uniqueunlimited & FileNameList) {
+static bool near pascal scancnames(uniqueunlimited *FileNameList) {
@@ line 454 -- CALL SITE, was never changed @@
-    MadeChanges |= updatelstfiles(PcbData.CmdLst,FileNameList,updatecmdlst);
+    MadeChanges |= updatelstfiles(PcbData.CmdLst,&FileNameList,updatecmdlst);
@@ line 457 -- CALL SITE, was never changed @@
-    MadeChanges |= scancnames(FileNameList);
+    MadeChanges |= scancnames(&FileNameList);
